/// This is copied from Cargokit (which is the official way to use it currently)
/// Details: https://fzyzcjy.github.io/flutter_rust_bridge/manual/integrate/builtin

Experimental repository to provide glue for seamlessly integrating cargo build
with flutter plugins and packages.

See https://matejknopp.com/post/flutter_plugin_in_rust_with_no_prebuilt_binaries/
for a tutorial on how to use Cargokit.

Example plugin available at https://github.com/irondash/hello_rust_ffi_plugin.

Kronoer changes to this copy (each marked "Kronoer (KRO-25)" in the code):

- run_build_tool.cmd exits with the build tool's exit code, so a failed Rust
  build fails Gradle instead of shipping an old library.
- gradle/plugin.gradle no longer adds android-x86 and android-x64 to debug
  builds; only the target platforms Flutter passes are built.
- build_tool/lib/src/android_environment.dart passes NDK tool paths with
  forward slashes on Windows, and there takes Perl and make for OpenSSL's
  build from MSYS2 (MSYS2_ROOT, default C:\msys64) unless OPENSSL_SRC_PERL
  is set.

